# Codex Adversarial Review

Target: branch diff against ba7706bc6d29b57090f6aba7fc1919cf16d18cbd
Verdict: needs-attention

No-ship: `/mapa` is now linked from primary navigation, but the page’s core map/viewer content is an empty placeholder, so users are sent to a route that cannot perform its advertised function.

Findings:
- [high] New public `/mapa` route ships with no map or index content (src/pages/MapaPage.tsx:43-50)
  `MapaPage` advertises a museum map experience, but the only section intended to render the actual viewer/index is empty and explicitly marked `filled in Plan 02`. Inference from the added navigation and route wiring: this incomplete page is now reachable from the main header and router, so production users can land on a route that promises floor navigation but provides no map, no floor selector, and no way to locate exhibits or services. That is a user-visible functional regression, not just missing polish.
  Recommendation: Do not expose `/mapa` until the viewer/index is implemented. Either render the actual map content from the added dataset/assets, or remove the route and header link from this change so users cannot navigate to an intentionally blank experience.

Next steps:
- Either complete the map viewer/index implementation before shipping, or revert the `/mapa` route and header entry from this change.
- Add a route-level test that asserts `/mapa` renders at least one floor map/image and corresponding index content so this cannot ship blank again.
